From: Josef Kubicek <josef.kubicek@braiins.cz>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: populate SSID on STA connect before country IE handling

When a mac80211-based driver (hwsim, ath9k, iwlwifi, etc.) connects as STA
using the authenticate+associate path (via wpa_supplicant), the SSID is never
stored in wdev->u.client.ssid. A fallback exists in __cfg80211_connect_result()
to extract it from the BSS IEs, but it's unreachable: it's placed after the
country IE lookup which returns early when no country IE is present.

Fix by moving the SSID extraction before the country IE handling.

--- a/net/wireless/sme.c	2026-04-04 19:02:32.655576000 +0300
+++ b/net/wireless/sme.c	2026-04-04 19:03:09.741977434 +0300
@@ -887,6 +887,22 @@ void __cfg80211_connect_result(struct ne
 
 	cfg80211_upload_connect_keys(wdev);
 
+	if (!wdev->u.client.ssid_len) {
+		const struct element *ssid;
+
+		rcu_read_lock();
+		for_each_valid_link(cr, link) {
+			ssid = ieee80211_bss_get_elem(cr->links[link].bss,
+						      WLAN_EID_SSID);
+			if (ssid && ssid->datalen) {
+				memcpy(wdev->u.client.ssid, ssid->data, ssid->datalen);
+				wdev->u.client.ssid_len = ssid->datalen;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+		rcu_read_unlock();
+	}
+
 	rcu_read_lock();
 	for_each_valid_link(cr, link) {
 		country_elem =
